      "text": "To find \\(\\mathbf{A}^{100}\\) for the matrix \\(\\mathbf{A} = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\end{pmatrix}\\), we will use the property of matrix exponentiation and cyclic permutations. First, let's compute a few powers of \\(\\mathbf{A}\\) to identify any patterns.\n\nCalculate \\(\\mathbf{A}^2\\):\n\\[\n\\mathbf{A}^2 = \\mathbf{A} \\cdot \\mathbf{A} = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\cdot 0 + 0 \\cdot 1 + 1 \\cdot 0 & 0 \\cdot 0 + 0 \\cdot 0 + 1 \\cdot 1 & 0 \\cdot 1 + 0 \\cdot 0 + 1 \\cdot 0 \\\\ 1 \\cdot 0 + 0 \\cdot 1 + 0 \\cdot 0 & 1 \\cdot 0 + 0 \\cdot 0 + 0 \\cdot 1 & 1 \\cdot 1 + 0 \\cdot 0 + 0 \\cdot 0 \\\\ 0 \\cdot 0 + 1 \\cdot 1 + 0 \\cdot 0 & 0 \\cdot 0 + 1 \\cdot 0 + 0 \\cdot 1 & 0 \\cdot 1 + 1 \\cdot 0 + 0 \\cdot 0 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\end{pmatrix} = -\\mathbf{A}.\n\\]\nSo, \\(\\mathbf{A}^2 = -\\mathbf{A}\\).\n\nNext, calculate \\(\\mathbf{A}^4\\):\n\\[\n\\mathbf{A}^4 = (\\mathbf{A}^2)^2 = (-\\mathbf{A})^2 = \\mathbf{A}^2 = -\\mathbf{A}.\n\\]\nWe observe that \\(\\mathbf{A}^4 = -\\mathbf{A}\\). This tells us that the powers of \\(\\mathbf{A}\\) repeat every 4 exponents. Specifically, \\(\\mathbf{A}^{4k} = (-1)^k \\mathbf{A}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{A}^{4k+1} = (-1)^{k+1} \\mathbf{A}\\), \\(\\mathbf{A}^{4k+2} = \\mathbf{A}\\), and \\(\\mathbf{A}^{4k+3} = \\mathbf{A}^2 = -\\mathbf{A}\\).\n\nTo find \\(\\mathbf{A}^{100}\\), we note that \\(100 = 4 \\cdot 25\\), so:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{A}^{100} = \\mathbf{A}^{4 \\cdot 25} = (\\mathbf{A}^4)^{25} = (-\\mathbf{A})^{25} = -(\\mathbf{A}^{25}) = -\\mathbf{A}^{25}.\n\\]\nNext, we need to find \\(\\mathbf{A}^{25}\\):\n\\[\n\\mathbf{A}^5 = \\mathbf{A} \\cdot \\mathbf{A}^4 = \\mathbf{A} \\cdot (-\\mathbf{A}) = -\\mathbf{A}^2 = -(-\\mathbf{A}) = \\mathbf{A}.\n\\]\nThus, \\(\\mathbf{A}^{25} = \\mathbf{A}\\). Therefore,\n\\[\n\\mathbf{A}^{100} = -\\mathbf{A}^{25} = -\\mathbf{A}.\n\\]\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\end{pmatrix}}.\n\\]",
